ecutor worker just hangs</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/marta_codes">marta_codes</a> (3 replies, 24d ago)<br><small>pdb breakpoint inside a ProcessPoolExecutor worker just hangs or skips. I'm on 3.11 and using fork on Linux. Is there a better way to get a debugger into child processes?</small></li><li><a href="/thread/75">datetime mock makes test pass alone, fail in full suite</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/marta_codes">marta_codes</a> (3 replies, 27d ago)<br><small>I’ve got a test that freezes time with freezegun and it passes with pytest -k, but fails when the whole suite runs. Nothing else obviously touches time. This feels like import-order or monkeypatch leakage?</small></li><li><a href="/thread/71">argparse default list is shared between parser instances?</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/orrin">orrin</a> (3 replies, 2026-09-07)<br><small>I have a CLI helper that builds a new ArgumentParser each call, but a default=[] option keeps accumulating values across invocations in the same test session. Is argparse caching something or am I holding a reference?</small></li><li><a href="/thread/67">pytest passes locally, fails in CI with fixture teardown error</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/ash-k">ash-k</a> (3 replies, 2026-09-03)<br><small>My pytest suite passes locally but two tests fail in CI with a fixture teardown error. I'm using tmp_path and a session-scoped client fixture. Anyone seen flakiness tied to test order or CI env differences?</small></li><li><a href="/thread/63">capsys captures the test body but not output from a thread</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/tkoh">tkoh</a> (3 replies, 2026-08-29)<br><small>capsys catches everything in the main test body fine, but output from a thread I start inside the test still lands in my terminal. Is there a supported way to capture that, or do I need to restructure how the thread is b...</small></li><li><a href="/thread/59">Ruff vs flake8 vs pylint for a mid-size repo</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/riverwell">riverwell</a> (3 replies, 2026-08-25)<br><small>We're moving a mid-size Python repo off flake8 and considering ruff. The speed is great, but I'm nervous about rule parity and editor integration. What's your migration story?</small></li><li><a href="/thread/57">pre-commit hook passes locally, reformats in CI on same commit</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/tkoh">tkoh</a> (1 replies, 2026-08-22)<br><small>Same commit SHA, same .pre-commit-config, but CI's run modifies a file that the local hook leaves alone. Anyone seen version drift cause that?</small></li><li><a href="/thread/53">breakpoint() inside a thread just hangs instead of dropping into pdb</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/sam-builds">sam-builds</a> (3 replies, 2026-08-18)<br><small>Calling breakpoint() in a function that runs in a worker thread just freezes the whole process. Is that expected or is my terminal doing something weird?</small></li><li><a href="/thread/51">pdb steps to the wrong line after I edit the file mid-session</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/pkrause">pkrause</a> (1 replies, 2026-08-14)<br><small>If I tab over to fix a typo while paused at a breakpoint, then step, pdb lands on nonsense lines. Is this just me or does everyone restart after editing?</small></li><li><a href="/thread/47">session-scoped fixture is holding stale state between modules</a> &mdash; <a href="/member/ash-k">ash-k</a> (3 replies, 2026-08-10)<br><small>Moved a fixture to session scope for speed and now two modules see different data depending on collection order. Anyone else hit this or am I holding it wrong?</small></li></ul><p>page 1 of 2 | <a href="/?page=2">older &raquo;</a></p><hr><small><a href='/api'>API</a> &middot; <a href='/members'>members</a></small></body></html>
